WHAT THE VIDEO CONFIG ADDS TO A KEY FRAME — attribution at 512x512, and the
first same-session three-arm split taken AFTER the ME SIMD chunk landed.

date:   2026-09-03
host:   mac — Apple M4 Pro, 12 logical cores, aarch64-apple-darwin. No foreign
        load: `ps` showed no other cargo/encoder process for the whole run.
commit: 22fd10e76 (main; the compute_stats row-pair change is the NEXT commit
        and is NOT in these numbers).
cell:   gradient 512x512 qp 40 preset 8, 8-bit 4:2:0. Both arms byte-identical
        to C at this cell (`ident=Y` in every perf_gate row below).
scale:  benchmarks/perf_2026-09-03-arm3-{still,videokey,inter}.tsv — paired
        interleaved, randomised order per round, 25 rounds/cell, all three
        arms run back to back in ONE session by ~/tmp/zsvt/arms.sh.
shares: /usr/bin/sample, 1 ms, 20 s steady state, 15.2-15.4 k leaf samples per
        arm per side. tools/perf_profile/{prof.sh,selftime.py,classify.py}.
data:   benchmarks/perf_videokey_attrib_2026-09-03.tsv

============ 1. THE THREE ARMS, SAME SESSION, POST-ME-SIMD =====================

The 2026-09-02 three-arm record measured its STILL arm in a different session
from its VIDEOKEY and INTER arms, and its INTER arm on a pre-SIMD binary. This
run measures all three back to back on one binary, so the subtraction below
carries no cross-session drift.

  preset 8, port ms / C ms (ratio)
  size   still                videokey              inter (2 frames)
   64    0.188 / 0.208 (0.90) 0.746 / 0.504 (1.49)  1.212 / 0.692 (1.76)
  128    0.494 / 0.333 (1.51) 2.392 / 1.039 (2.34)  3.318 / 1.371 (2.43)
  256    2.739 / 1.091 (2.53) 10.255 / 3.459 (2.95) 12.816 / 4.290 (2.99)
  512   10.439 / 3.854 (2.71) 50.326 / 15.967 (3.14) 62.891 / 19.147 (3.29)*
  slope-ratio  2.81x               3.21x                 3.23x

  (* the 512 INTER cell is ident=N — it compares two encoders making different
  decisions — and is excluded from the inter fit, as in every prior record.)

DIFFERENCING THE ARMS (a subtraction of measured quantities, never a
projection) splits the port's excess over C on an inter cell three ways:

  size  still key frame   video config on it   the inter frame   total excess
   64    -0.020  (-3.8%)   +0.262  (50.4%)      +0.278  (53.5%)    0.520
  128    +0.161   (8.3%)   +1.192  (61.2%)      +0.594  (30.5%)    1.947
  256    +1.648  (19.3%)   +5.148  (60.4%)      +1.730  (20.3%)    8.526
  512    +6.585  (15.1%)   +27.774 (63.5%)      +9.385  (21.5%)   43.744

**CORRECTION TO THE STANDING FIGURE.** docs/perf-status.md and four agent
briefs quote "44-52 % of the port's excess on an inter cell is the video-mode
key frame". That was measured BEFORE the ME SIMD chunk. The ME work cut the
inter frame 1.75x and left the key frame untouched, so the key frame's share
ROSE: it is now **50-64 %** (50.4 / 61.2 / 60.4 / 63.5 at 64/128/256/512 p8),
and the inter frame's share FELL from 35 % to 20-21 % at 256 and above. The
video-mode key frame is now the largest component at every size except 64x64,
where it ties the inter frame.

The video config costs the port 3.09x (256) and 3.29x (512) what it costs C —
higher than the still key frame's own 2.53x / 2.71x, so it is not merely "more
of the same work".

============ 2. WHAT THAT ADD IS MADE OF, BY CLASS (512x512 p8) ================

port delta = videokey_ms - still_ms on the port; C delta likewise on C. The
port's deltas sum to 39.4 ms against the 39.887 ms the paired gate measures for
the same subtraction, i.e. the profile accounts for ~99 % of it.

