  +0.321  COEFF_WRITE   av1_write_coeffs_txb_1d

============ 3. FOUR THINGS THIS SAYS THAT THE 256x256 RECORD DID NOT ==========

(a) **QUANT_RDOQ IS NOT A LEVER.** It is the port's second-largest addition in
    absolute ms (5.66) but its ratio is **1.66x** — the closest to parity of
    any class here, and `optimize_b` (3.87) faces `svt_aom_quantize_inv_quantize`
    (3.00), 1.29x. Ranking by absolute self time puts it second; ranking by
    EXCESS puts it sixth. Rank by excess.

(b) **ALLOC IS THE THIRD-LARGEST ITEM AND C'S IS ZERO.** The video config adds
    2.69 ms of allocator work to the port (`_xzm_free` 1.28,
    `_xzm_malloc_zone_malloc_type_calloc_entry` 0.26, `madvise` 0.24,
    `_xzm_xzone_malloc` 0.22, tail) and **0.000 ms** to C — every symbol on C's
    side is below the 0.02 ms cut. Add LIBC_MEM (`__bzero` 0.71,
    `_platform_memmove` 0.66, `_platform_memset` 0.62) and the memory-traffic
    pair is 4.24 ms, 15.3 % of the excess. NOT MEASURED: which structure. The
    still path's own allocation work was measured NULL when pooled
    (benchmarks/alloc_bufpool_null_2026-08-13.meta — do not re-run that
    experiment), but this is a DIFFERENT population: buffers the video config
    turns on (recon, post-filter staging, LR/CDEF search state), not the
    per-block decision Vecs that experiment pooled.

(c) **CDEF's ratio is 9.92x, the worst of any class**, and it is 11.8 % of the
    excess — bigger than LOOP_RESTORE. `cdef_filter_block` (1.556) is already
    NEON on both sides, so it is a QUALITY item; `cdef_find_dir` (0.709) is a
    coverage gap, verified scalar by source read (crates/svtav1-dsp/src/cdef.rs
    has no `incant!`/`#[arcane]` anywhere near it) against C's
    `svt_aom_cdef_find_dir_8bit_neon` (cdef_block_neon.c:348).

(d) **The still-path SIMD queue and this list are the same list.** Every entry
    in docs/perf-status.md's ranked coverage queue appears here, which is what
    the 2026-09-02 record predicted; what is new is that CDEF outranks loop
    restoration at 512x512 and that ALLOC — which is not in that queue at all —
    outranks both `dr_predictor_edged` and `cdef_find_dir`.

============ IS THIS NUMBER DEFENSIBLE ========================================

* The profile accounts for 99 % of the paired subtraction on the port side
  (39.44 profiled vs 39.887 measured) and 93 % on C's (11.30 vs 12.113); the
  shortfall on C is the |delta| < 0.02 ms row cut, which drops more rows from
  the smaller side.
* Both harnesses loop init -> encode -> teardown; >99 % of samples land in the
  timed region on both sides at this cell (checked at the top of each call
  graph, per tools/perf_profile/README.md trap 2).
* The shares are multiplied by the PAIRED gate ms, never by a stopwatch on the
  profiling run (trap 3).
* `<deduplicated_symbol>` is re-parented by selftime.py (trap 1).
* SINGLE CELL. 512x512 p8 only. The class ORDER differs from the 2026-09-02
  256x256 record (CDEF and ALLOC move up), so do not treat either ordering as
  size-independent.
